<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ordos Plateau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ordos Plateau is a high, partly desert region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, enclosed on three sides by the great northern loop of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> and now mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>. A frontier between Chinese farmers and steppe peoples, it was contested by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> and the Han, settled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-xiongnu">Southern Xiongnu</a> and later by Tangut groups, and gives its name to the Ordos bronzes of the steppe animal style.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ordos-plateau.jpg" alt="Ordos Plateau" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shannon; derivative work by Zcm11 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yellowrivermap_copy_copy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
